//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- T10.1: the three confidence controls
//
// These are not recall queries and are deliberately excluded from recall@1 and
// recall@k — they carry no `expected_session_prefix` because two of them are
// asserting that the right answer is **nothing**. They are judged on their own
// by `--controls`, and a failure there fails the run.
//
// Why they exist. The agent audit of 23 aug 2026 found that `find` could not
// tell a topic the archive answers from one it has never heard of: 0.01836
// against 0.01639 on the reference archive, 1.12x apart, because reciprocal
// rank fusion is a function of rank alone. T10.1 added a second axis and a
// floor. These three are what stop it rotting: one query the archive answers,
// which must come back `strong`; one topic that is definitively absent and
// whose words nevertheless all appear in the corpus separately, which must
// come back with zero rows; and one string of invented words, which must come
// back with zero rows for the simpler reason that fts5 finds no term at all.
//
// The audit's own controls could not be reused. Its nonsense string had been
// written down in a document that was then indexed, so by the time anyone
// re-ran it the archive contained the session that typed it and the control
// matched itself. That is the failure mode a control has: publication. These
// three are safe against it in the only way that lasts — they are scored
// against `evals/fixture/`, a corpus generated by `scripts/make-eval-corpus.mjs`
// from a template grid, which nothing anybody types can ever get into.
{"query": "pgbouncer transaction pooling", "control": "strong", "class": "control", "note": "TRUE TOPIC, short and distinctive — the corpus has a session about exactly this. Must return at least one row at `strong`. This is the control that fails if the floor is ever raised until nothing survives it: an honest empty is only worth having if the tool can still say yes."}
{"query": "kubernetes ingress payment service", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "ABSENT TOPIC, and the point is that its words are not absent — the corpus has sessions about payments and about services, so bm25 returns rows and ranks them, and before T10.1 the top one scored inside 12% of a true phrase hit. Must return ZERO rows. If this ever returns anything, the cliff has become a ranking again."}
{"query": "vondrelic pashtomeer", "control": "no-match", "class": "control", "note": "INVENTED WORDS, generated for this file and used nowhere else. Must return ZERO rows, and it already did before T10.1 — fts5 finds no term, so there is nothing to rank. It is here as a regression control rather than as a fix: the audit reported that gibberish returned ten confident rows, that claim did not reproduce on uncontaminated tokens, and this is what keeps it from becoming true later."}
